#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175733 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e09c5b9-5f31-52a5-b696-b2df1879d289" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Rational Equations Containing a Binomial in One Denominator"}] :question/id #uuid "1be25af9-d59f-5270-b9e1-d0c5dcd731e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-14143" :question/problem "Solve $\\dfrac{2}{1-2k}=-\\dfrac{4}{3k}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $k=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and $k=0$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{2}{1-2k}&=-\\dfrac{4}{3k}\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{2}{1-2k}&=\\dfrac{-4}{3k}\\[5pt]\n\t\t2 \\cdot 3k &= (-4) \\cdot (1-2k)\\[5pt]\t\t\n\t\t6k&=-4+8k\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\t\n\t\t6k&=-4+8k\\[5pt]\n\t\t6k-8k &=-4+8k-8k\\[5pt]\n\t\t-2k&=-4\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{-2k}{-2} &= \\dfrac{-4}{-2} \\[5pt]\n\t\tk &= 2\n\t}\n$$\n\nSince  $k =   2$ is different from $k=0$ and $k=\\dfrac{1}{2}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175734 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "208596d0-1a45-57b2-afa5-d17e99218e38" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Rational Equations Containing Binomials in Both Denominators"}] :question/id #uuid "72cf8733-9727-5a9f-8028-1dee62e5715d" :question/math-academy-id "e-14146" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{2}{4x+12}=\\dfrac{2}{x+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $x=-3$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\dfrac{2}{4x+12} &= \\dfrac{2}{x+3} \\\t\n\t2 \\cdot (x+3) &= (4x+12) \\cdot 2 \\\n\t2x + 6 &= 8x + 24\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t2x + 6 &= 8x + 24 \\\n\t2x + 6-24 &= 8x + 24-24 \\\n\t2x-18 &= 8x \\\n\t2x-18-2x &= 8x-2x \\\n\t-18 &= 6x \\\n        \\dfrac{-18}{6} &= \\dfrac{6x}{6} \\\n        -3 &= x\n\t}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-3$ cannot be a solution, the equation has **no solutions.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175739 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f3e1fc3-c46b-5958-92b2-0f2dc11ff961" :knowledge-point/title "Equations Containing Negative Signs"}] :question/id #uuid "2d5b690c-bee9-5503-8f21-285b8c42d5fa" :question/math-academy-id "e-14705" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $-\\dfrac{3}{2x}=\\dfrac{2}{x+7}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $x=0$ and $x=-7$  cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t-\\dfrac{3}{2x}&=\\dfrac{2}{x+7}\\[5pt]\t\n        \\dfrac{-3}{2x}&=\\dfrac{2}{x+7}\\[5pt]\t\n\t(-3) \\cdot (x+7) &=2x \\cdot (2) \\[5pt]\t\n\t-3x - 21&=  4x\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t-3x - 21&= 4x\\[5pt]\t\n\t-3x -21 + 3x&=4x + 3x\\[5pt]\t\n\t-21&=7x\\[5pt]\t\n\t\\dfrac{-21}{7}&=\\dfrac{7x}{7} \\[5pt]\t\n\t-3 &= x\n\t}\n$$\n\nSince  $x =   - 3$ is different from $x=0$ and $x=-7$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x= -3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "208596d0-1a45-57b2-afa5-d17e99218e38" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Rational Equations Containing Binomials in Both Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33babf07-c160-55a4-a57e-8f1f026442aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497910} {:answer/id #uuid "5622a314-ef0f-58ee-82bf-08d1195bd0d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498001} {:answer/id #uuid "6c385abf-1bdc-5e1c-9a5a-9c43590eb776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498063} {:answer/id #uuid "962e7a6e-9daa-52cd-b057-92b6a3276624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498142} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7a97d8-953d-58e7-8bd4-4c2c06e494c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "962e7a6e-9daa-52cd-b057-92b6a3276624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498142} :answer-field/id #uuid "e46b1ed4-dc5b-5ee9-9e2f-0d84b2d0b493" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f11ebff6-3ffc-5ee8-b046-9fea0d3fb648" :question/math-academy-id "q-102820" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\frac{1}{y+2}=\\frac{3}{2y+5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $y=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $y=-2$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y+2} & =\\frac{3}{2y+5} \\\\ 1\\cdot (2y+5) & =(y+2)\\cdot 3 \\\\ 2y+5 & =3y+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y+5 & =3y+6 \\\\ 2y+5-2y & =3y+6-2y \\\\ 5 & =y+6 \\\\ 5-6 & =y+6-6 \\\\ -1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $y=-1$ is different from $y=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $y=-2,$ we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $y=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "208596d0-1a45-57b2-afa5-d17e99218e38" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Rational Equations Containing Binomials in Both Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b979e065-920d-5c3f-a304-5e466652e958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b979e065-920d-5c3f-a304-5e466652e958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498212} :answer-field/id #uuid "219bd34f-9e71-5315-809c-74bdaa997dcb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "498a8787-d5a7-5977-8e3c-6512904632e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-212151" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{1}{x-2}=\\frac{2}{x+4}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $x=-4$ and $x=2$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x-2} & =\\frac{2}{x+4} \\\\ 1\\cdot (x+4) & =(x-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ x+4 & =2x-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4 & =2x-4 \\\\ x+4-x & =2x-4-x \\\\ 4 & =x-4 \\\\ 4+4 & =x-4+4 \\\\ 8 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=8$ is different from $x=-4$ and $x=2,$ we can accept it as a solution. Therefore, the solution is $x=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e09c5b9-5f31-52a5-b696-b2df1879d289" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Rational Equations Containing a Binomial in One Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "331b3a46-4dde-58b0-8ee2-aa402b36e943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "331b3a46-4dde-58b0-8ee2-aa402b36e943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497907} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4569325-3c4a-56d0-897e-ce1619017f40" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "55ccf1ca-e318-559b-93b2-d5adb07323fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-214969" :question/problem "Solve for $z$ where $\\frac{4}{3z-4}=\\frac{2}{z}.$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $z=0$ and $z=\\frac{4}{3}$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3z-4} & =\\frac{2}{z} \\\\ 4\\cdot z & =(3z-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 4z & =6z-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4z & =6z-8 \\\\ 4z-6z & =6z-8-6z \\\\ -2z & =-8 \\\\ \\frac{-2z}{-2} & =\\frac{-8}{-2} \\\\ z & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z=4$ is different from $z=0$ and $z=\\frac{4}{3}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $z=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f3e1fc3-c46b-5958-92b2-0f2dc11ff961" :knowledge-point/title "Equations Containing Negative Signs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea5fc96b-2881-5ff1-a515-566e2d5417e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea5fc96b-2881-5ff1-a515-566e2d5417e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498314} :answer-field/id #uuid "d21bbdd2-fa29-5007-b862-173cef502ae2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22fb2eb0-0b37-5e4e-b13e-bbd075981dde" :question/math-academy-id "q-215066" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{4}{3x-5}=-\\frac{2}{x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $x=\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=0$  cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3x-5} & =-\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3x-5} & =\\frac{-2}{x} \\\\ 4\\cdot x & =(3x-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 4x & =-6x+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =-6x+10 \\\\ 4x+6x & =-6x+10+6x \\\\ 10x & =10 \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & =\\frac{10}{10} \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=1$ is different from $x=\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=0,$ we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f3e1fc3-c46b-5958-92b2-0f2dc11ff961" :knowledge-point/title "Equations Containing Negative Signs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30744542-cd30-586c-a63e-1ad741fff562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497900} {:answer/id #uuid "37136d31-8172-51ad-a5c0-797a56d40b70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497921} {:answer/id #uuid "7a49664b-0618-5bce-88b5-7c3bb92808fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498092} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4240a1-f2a7-58b4-a361-69a6a94af703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498122} {:answer/id #uuid "eb155907-2c21-5258-bfc6-144370883337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30744542-cd30-586c-a63e-1ad741fff562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497900} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae3890f1-aded-5a97-97dd-fdc9f98201d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df156dc2-1100-5e24-8d9b-7d140c269cdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-215111" :question/problem "Solve for $y$ where $\\frac{3}{y}=-\\frac{2}{y+5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $y=0$ and $y=-5$  cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{y} & =-\\frac{2}{y+5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{y} & =\\frac{-2}{y+5} \\\\ 3\\cdot (y+5) & =y\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 3y+15 & =-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y+15 & =-2y \\\\ 3y+15-3y & =-2y-3y \\\\ 15 & =-5y \\\\ \\frac{15}{-5} & =\\frac{-5y}{-5} \\\\ -3 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $y=-3$ is different from $y=0$ and $y=-5$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $y=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "208596d0-1a45-57b2-afa5-d17e99218e38" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Rational Equations Containing Binomials in Both Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf7fb25c-7e01-5e0a-bb68-7220204953b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf7fb25c-7e01-5e0a-bb68-7220204953b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498225} :answer-field/id #uuid "0be943a0-79a0-5c05-acad-f4e1a7056cf1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f1e58eb-509a-57ef-98db-701046002754" :question/math-academy-id "q-215142" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{2}{x+8}=\\frac{3}{5-2x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $x=-8$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{x+8} & =\\frac{3}{5-2x} \\\\ 2\\cdot (5-2x) & =(x+8)\\cdot 3 \\\\ 10-4x & =3x+24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10-4x & =3x+24 \\\\ 10-4x+4x & =3x+24+4x \\\\ 10 & =7x+24 \\\\ 10-24 & =7x+24-24 \\\\ -14 & =7x \\\\ \\frac{-14}{7} & =\\frac{7x}{7} \\\\ -2 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-2$ is different from $x=-8$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2},$ we can accept it as a solution. Therefore, the solution is $x=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e09c5b9-5f31-52a5-b696-b2df1879d289" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Rational Equations Containing a Binomial in One Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c6b1223-0634-58ec-9b69-cb2b95bd6ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497892} {:answer/id #uuid "2db540c3-141c-593c-869b-521603917aa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497897} {:answer/id #uuid "34452f5b-bcd7-5a09-b420-1122b2a1b1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497912} {:answer/id #uuid "62ab66f6-4b19-58f6-8eee-1ca280768832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498035} {:answer/id #uuid "c594295e-dea8-5d8b-b79a-e56856ef5d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c6b1223-0634-58ec-9b69-cb2b95bd6ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497892} :answer-field/id #uuid "7adb7269-978f-5ee2-893c-a998f4e58535" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e6d0052-ede1-5485-af6f-3596ff037aef" :question/math-academy-id "q-47793" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{3}{2x}=\\frac{4}{3x-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2x} & =\\frac{4}{3x-1} \\\\ 3\\cdot (3x-1) & =(2x)\\cdot 4 \\\\ 9x-3 & =8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-3 & =8x \\\\ 9x-3-9x & =8x-9x \\\\ -3 & =-x \\\\ \\frac{-3}{-1} & =\\frac{-x}{-1} \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=3$ is different from $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3},$ we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is  $x=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498563 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "208596d0-1a45-57b2-afa5-d17e99218e38" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Rational Equations Containing Binomials in Both Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49a171aa-6934-5617-97f6-64f6404f7903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497967} {:answer/id #uuid "5a86d0f7-5212-525a-a475-11d2e4066320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498013} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd83a26-a78b-518a-b425-85fc64f2d1ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498121} {:answer/id #uuid "df852c33-4c97-5a41-a460-eb0f7cc68cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498299} {:answer/id #uuid "fe569451-7d21-5b9c-95e6-a761246542b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49a171aa-6934-5617-97f6-64f6404f7903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497967} :answer-field/id #uuid "3854452e-f405-5681-9b94-d9ccc3fdd0fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93eae023-b2fa-5964-961a-3ebb3b808918" :question/math-academy-id "q-51492" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\frac{5}{4x+24}=\\frac{5}{x+6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $x=-6$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4x+24} & =\\frac{5}{x+6} \\\\ 5\\cdot (x+6) & =(4x+24)\\cdot 5 \\\\ 5x+30 & =20x+120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+30 & =20x+120 \\\\ 5x+30-5x & =20x+120-5x \\\\ 30 & =15x+120 \\\\ 30-120 & =15x+120-120 \\\\ -90 & =15x \\\\ \\frac{-90}{15} & =\\frac{15x}{15} \\\\ -6 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-6$ cannot be a solution, the equation has no solutions."}]}
